MODIFICATIONS (GPLv3 section 5a)
================================================================================

Modified by Ben Meadors on 2026-08-15.

Fork point: tobychui/DezKVM-Go commit 7195239e557747784d0da68eb2be6d2cc6bb4e9b
(2026-08-07). Changes relative to that commit:

Added
  firmware/                   ESP32-S3 firmware (ESP-IDF + TinyUSB). Presents a
                              boot-protocol HID keyboard and an absolute mouse to
                              the target, and accepts CH9329-compatible frames
                              from the host on UART0 at 115200. New work, GPLv3.
                              Deviates from byte-faithful CH9329 emulation in two
                              documented places; see docs/PROTOCOL.md section 7.
  tools/ch9329_test.py        Protocol test harness. New work, GPLv3.
  tools/verify_descriptors.py USB descriptor validator. New work, GPLv3.
  docs/PROTOCOL.md            The CH9329 wire protocol as the UI actually speaks
                              it, extracted from docs/local-kvm.js. New work.
  NOTICE                      This file.

Changed
  docs/local-kvm.js           Added the MS2130 capture dongle (534d:2130,
  src/www/local-kvm.js        345f:2130) to supportedVidPidPairs, ahead of the
                              existing MS2109 entries which are retained. Added a
                              1080p60 entry to MODE_LIST for the MS2130. Reworded
                              two MS2109-specific console/toast messages to refer
                              to the capture device generically.

  docs/settings.html          Reworded the HID Baudrate field description: this
  src/www/settings.html       firmware always starts at 115200, so the CH9329
                              9600-baud reconfiguration step does not apply. The
                              9600 option itself is retained for use with real
                              CH9329 hardware. Updated the About tab's supported
                              hardware list from MS2109 + CH9329 to MS2130 +
                              ESP32-S3, noting both older parts still work.

  src/update_githubpage.sh    The clean step now preserves docs/PROTOCOL.md,
                              which lives in docs/ but is not part of the served
                              UI and would otherwise be deleted on every sync.

  README.md                   Rewritten for this hardware and setup flow.

Removed
  PCB/                        Not copied. See below.
  3D Models/
  img/                        Upstream product photography, not applicable here.


================================================================================
HARDWARE ASSETS DELIBERATELY NOT INCLUDED
================================================================================

Upstream licenses its hardware assets -- the PCB/ and "3D Models/" directories --
under Creative Commons BY-NC-ND (Attribution, NonCommercial, NoDerivatives).
NoDerivatives means they may not be modified and redistributed, so they are not
copied into this repository in any form, modified or otherwise.

This project does not need them: it uses a stock ESP32-S3 dev board and an
off-the-shelf HDMI capture dongle. Obtain the reference hardware from upstream
under its own terms.


